<article class="env-example" id="08WN">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08WN">Example <span data-tag="08WN">35.4.7</span>.</a> For a ring $R$ and $f_1, \ldots , f_ n \in R$ generating the unit ideal, the morphism $R \to R_{f_1} \oplus \ldots \oplus R_{f_ n}$ is universally injective. Although this is immediate from Lemma <a href="/tag/08WP" data-tag="08WP">35.4.8</a>, it is instructive to check it directly: we immediately reduce to the case where $R$ is local, in which case some $f_ i$ must be a unit and so the map $R \to R_{f_ i}$ is an isomorphism. </p>
</article>